lighthouse-l Digest                  Saturday, September 4 1999
Volume 03 : Issue 198

Today's Topics:
   1. [forum] Cape Sorrow, 2182 kHz, tonight. Recording. (eward)
   2. [forum] Re: Cape Sorrow (keeper)
   3. [forum] Re: Cape Sorrow (qrp_anna)

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Message: 1
From: eward
Subject: [forum] Cape Sorrow, 2182 kHz, tonight. Recording.
Thread: /forum/signals/thread_041.html

I drove down to Cape Sorrow tonight on a hunch after LB-204 and LB-208.
Parked on the access road below the old light around 2230.
At 2310 local, on 2182, a voice. Not a carrier. A voice.
"Cape Sorrow, Cape Sorrow, Cape Sorrow. This is Cape Sorrow radio.
The light is out. I say again, the light is out." Then "four seven,
four seven." Then nothing.
I got it on tape. It's uploaded as /signals/CS-0903.wav and logged as LB-212.
My hands are still shaking. The station has been dead since 1987.
Please listen and tell me I'm not crazy.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Message: 2
From: keeper
Subject: [forum] Re: Cape Sorrow

Eli, I just listened three times with headphones. I don't know what
to say. That's the best thing anyone has ever posted here.
Everybody: log 2182 tonight and tomorrow, wherever you are.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Message: 3
From: qrp_anna
Subject: [forum] Re: Cape Sorrow

goosebumps. actual goosebumps.

End of lighthouse-l Digest V3 #198
**********************************

