@@@ mail-mara-list-1022
type: email
title: going dark
author: keeper
date: 1999-10-22T21:00:00-07:00
path: /mail/keeper/1999-10-22_going-dark.eml
role: critical
---
From: Mara Quinlan <keeper@beacon.lighthouse.net>
To: Mara Quinlan <keeper@beacon.lighthouse.net>
Bcc: (64 recipients, old lighthouse-l address list)
Date: Fri, 22 Oct 1999 21:00:00 -0700
Subject: going dark

Dear all,

By now most of you know the server died on the 17th and Ray could
only save a fraction of it. Please don't be hard on him. He has
been hard enough on himself.

I also want to be honest about one thing. Before the move, on the
16th, I removed some material from the site myself. I made that
decision for reasons I believe were right, and I'm not going to
explain them here, because the explanation belongs to someone else.
The two things are not connected. I know that's hard to believe.

I don't think I have it in me to rebuild. The Lighthouse Network
is going dark. Thank you for two and a half years of listening.

Log what you heard, not what you hoped to hear.

Mara

